{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191185-cabal-theme-shadow-name","id":1191185,"title":"Cabal Theme/Shadow Name","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-02T18:24:42-08:00","id":1191185,"title":"Cabal Theme/Shadow Name","content":"So I'm at an impasse as a GM slightly. I'm trying to get a game off the ground, and my players are thinking about maybe in play working out a cabal theme as they find their footings and buying the relevant merit. However, since this would also strongly encourage thematic shadow names, their doing after char gen (possibly even well after if they wait an arc or so to do this) means they're certainly not going to have well coordinated Shadow Names. I'm not even sure how a cabal theme would exist without the Shadow Names helping feed into it, honestly since it specifically is about boosting their own use of that merit.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have some suggestions on this? Maybe have them try to re-tailor the behavior or physical presentation of their shadow identities or something to make the theme work? This is a really minor, mostly superficial narrative thing but it is causing a weird personal stumbling block in my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T18:39:17-08:00","id":1191190,"title":"","content":"Hmm, but wouldn\u2019t \u201cI am A of the B cabal\u201d be enough of a persona to justify the Yantra? Not sure if I understood the issue here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T18:46:25-08:00","id":1191191,"title":"","content":"They're debating like five themes and go all in with names, but since they're at a deadlock of no commitment to anything in particular they're thinking of working it out in character.<br /> <br /> All of them however seem to like the idea of themed names too. My personal favorite was the famous philosophers one. Post char gen, you don't really change your Shadow Name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T18:49:26-08:00","id":1191192,"title":"","content":"Sure you can. <br /> I have. <br /> It's a good way to represent a change in perspective or focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T18:56:46-08:00","id":1191195,"title":"","content":"It shouldn\u2019t be that much trouble as long as the names/themes aren\u2019t blatantly contradictory.<br /> <br /> In-universe, Cabal Theme might help expand a mage\u2019s Shadow Name symbolism. Dawn, an Obrimos whose magical theme was that of literal light, might add \u201cthe dawn breaks after the deepest dark\u201d to her theme after joining a cabal named the Hanged Men, allowing her to invoke her Shadow Name on magic to grant hope and willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T19:29:59-08:00","id":1191207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191185-cabal-theme-shadow-name?p=1191195#post1191195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It shouldn\u2019t be that much trouble as long as the names/themes aren\u2019t blatantly contradictory.<br /> <br /> In-universe, Cabal Theme might help expand a mage\u2019s Shadow Name symbolism. Dawn, an Obrimos whose magical theme was that of literal light, might add \u201cthe dawn breaks after the deepest dark\u201d to her theme after joining a cabal named the Hanged Men, allowing her to invoke her Shadow Name on magic to grant hope and willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely good point, I think I just was overthinking this and panicked a little bit since I've GM'd a lot of games in the past but never a CofD game. I always struggle a lot to find ways as a GM to help promote atmosphere and theme, and sometimes it clicks and sometimes it doesn't, so given how heavy a CofD game can be on thematics and little flourishes to make the world feel right I may be working myself into a knot when it really need not be.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T21:06:09-08:00","id":1191226,"title":"","content":"You can also just tell them that they can build their characters as normal as if without a cabal theme in mind, and as they develop a theme in character they're allowed to alter their Shadow Names to fit the theme. It makes sense to me, Mages usually expect to end up in a cabal, but that doesn't mean they know what kind of symbolism they're going to be working with so establishing a personal identity takes precedence until they get more comfortable working together as a group and modify their identity to fit the new dynamic.<br /> <br /> You should also feel free to give your own thoughts on what their group might be about based on the actions they take in the game.<br /> <br /> As a pseudo-example, I have a friend who's been running a game for years. His group although an established cabal have never chosen a name for themselves. The Consilium has ended up giving them an unofficial name though, the Golden Road. As in, the road to Hell is paved with good (gold) intentions. They mean well, but overall they're highly individualistic and are a definite wild card in Consilium politics and frequently cause chaos as a result. They'd probably be justified in picking up the Cabal Theme Merit and using it for things that fit that definition of their group that's been laid on them by outsiders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T04:02:31-08:00","id":1191301,"title":"","content":"In my limited mage experience, mages do change shadow names. In my own setting/head canon this is pretty common.<br /> Mages usually choose their own or is appointed a shadow name by their mentors, however like identity in real life it's bound to be changes in it. Developing or changing it outright to fit would be possible and appropriate. Exploring your own supernal reflection and thinking about whom you really are and want to be is sure to bring changes. Usually this comes with greater understanding, dramatic changes in perspective and ones life or increased knowledge and understanding. This could happen for example when you gain a new title or position within the Consilium or Order or when gaining Gnosis. In my mind, if a new dot of Gnosis is enough to change your Virtue or Vice one should consider if ones Shadow Name is still fitting for the 'new' you. In that you also get a new, or can get a completely new Nimbus as well speaks highly to the possibility that your supernal identity can change dramatically when gaining deeper understanding of the cosmos. <br /> Not to say that every, or even most mages change their Shadow Names, but surely enough to be considered common.<br /> <br /> Cabal theme, as with the merit, is a cabal that is highly themed around some form of concept and every member is either one part of that or a symbol of the idea in general, their practice and collective identity strengthening each other. What this theme is should probably be talked about before making the characters so each can fit but if they don't surely they can find common ground in character while playing it out. <br /> However if we got some short descriptions of the player characters and their shadow names, we might give some inspiration of possible themes.<br /> <br /> Some examples of themed cabals in my own games include The Augurs, a cabal themed with prophecy, foretelling and omen reading made up by members of the guardians and the mysterium, all taking Shadow Names from famous oracles, prophets and the like. Another themed cabal is The Unknown Hand, themed with shadow manipulation of sleeper society and guardian labyrinths members taking Shadow Names corresponding to subtlety, changes, and manipulation. The Brotherhood of the Rune-carver is themed around Nordic mythology and the old sagas connection to the myth of the Awakened city, with names taken corresponding to different parts of old Norse myths and life.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T06:00:47-08:00","id":1191324,"title":"","content":"Maybe they don't have Shadow Names? There ought to be some &quot;John Doe&quot; term used to address initiates who have been inducted into the Pentacle on some level but have yet to choose a shadow name, probably varying by order. Make up a couple of those and let them figure out the proper ones as you go.<br /> <br /> Could even spin it into a theme for the initial stretch of the chronicle; the characters have gotten to the point of being ready to form a cabal without having decided what they actually want to do in life (as symbolized by the lack of Shadow Names), but their mentors are tired of their waffling and have kicked them out into the real world to figure it out. They'll have to prove themselves, find identity and purpose yada yada coming of age story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T06:34:50-08:00","id":1191328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191185-cabal-theme-shadow-name?p=1191324#post1191324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe they don't have Shadow Names? There ought to be some &quot;John Doe&quot; term used to address initiates who have been inducted into the Pentacle on some level but have yet to choose a shadow name, probably varying by order. Make up a couple of those and let them figure out the proper ones as you go.<br /> <br /> Could even spin it into a theme for the initial stretch of the chronicle; the characters have gotten to the point of being ready to form a cabal without having decided what they actually want to do in life (as symbolized by the lack of Shadow Names), but their mentors are tired of their waffling and have kicked them out into the real world to figure it out. They'll have to prove themselves, find identity and purpose yada yada coming of age story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the Orders actually allow mages to go without Shadow Names? I mean, it\u2019s basically your social identity among the Awakened. I thought mages start with an \u2018empty\u2019 Shadow Name, one that sounds fancy and meaningful but without the effort to truly harness that meaning, represented by not actually having dots in the Shadow Name Merit. <br /> <br /> Regardless, the idea of getting yourself a proper Shadow Name, likely one that fits your first cabal to bond with, is excellent as early chronicle material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T07:05:42-08:00","id":1191334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191185-cabal-theme-shadow-name?p=1191328#post1191328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does the Orders actually allow mages to go without Shadow Names? I mean, it\u2019s basically your social identity among the Awakened. I thought mages start with an \u2018empty\u2019 Shadow Name, one that sounds fancy and meaningful but without the effort to truly harness that meaning, represented by not actually having dots in the Shadow Name Merit.<br /> <br /> Regardless, the idea of getting yourself a proper Shadow Name, likely one that fits your first cabal to bond with, is excellent as early chronicle material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not aware of any material that specifies one way or another, which generally puts it in &quot;it's up to you&quot; territory. I'm just thinking that since using someone's sympathetic name is a big no-no but a Shadow Name isn't something you take on lightly, it's reasonable to assume there's some tradition regarding how you address a mage who has been inducted into Awakened society but doesn't yet have a Shadow Name.<br /> <br /> Probably multiple different traditions, actually, depending on time, place and order. Just making them pick one as soon as possible is probably a popular option, but it's not unreasonable to say that for whatever reason, this particular Consilium has a tradition of referring to un-Named mages with generic terms like &quot;Initiate Four&quot; and legislation in place to keep the names from &quot;sticking&quot; to any person.<br /> <br /> There's a specific point of conflict if you want it, actually; the council is cross with the PCs because they're approaching the maximum allotted time a Mage is allowed to go with a generic Name. The Lex Magica doesn't actually specify what happens if they overstay the time limit and it's never come up before <i>because everyone else in this Consilium is a responsible adult making responsible adult decisions, Initiate Three</i>, but it's sure to be very embarrassing for everyone involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T07:10:01-08:00","id":1191335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Terrorforge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191185-cabal-theme-shadow-name?p=1191334#post1191334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not aware of any material that specifies one way or another, which generally puts it in &amp;quot;it's up to you&amp;quot; territory. I'm just thinking that since using someone's sympathetic name is a big no-no but a Shadow Name isn't something you take on lightly, it's reasonable to assume there's some tradition regarding how you address a mage who has been inducted into Awakened society but doesn't yet have a Shadow Name.<br /> <br /> Probably multiple different traditions, actually, depending on time, place and order. Just making them pick one as soon as possible is probably a popular option, but it's not unreasonable to say that for whatever reason, this particular Consilium has a tradition of referring to un-Named mages with generic terms like &amp;quot;Initiate Four&amp;quot; and legislation in place to keep the names from &amp;quot;sticking&amp;quot; to any person.<br /> <br /> There's a specific point of conflict if you want it, actually; the council is cross with the PCs because they're approaching the maximum allotted time a Mage is allowed to go with a generic Name. The Lex Magica doesn't actually specify what happens if they overstay the time limit and it's never come up before <i>because everyone else in this Consilium is a responsible adult making responsible adult decisions, Initiate Three</i>, but it's sure to be very embarrassing for everyone involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what, the last sentence is evocative enough to make me revoke what I said just earlier. This should totally be allowed. (Though I imagine it comes up more with Seers, since they\u2019re both authoritatian and place huge importance on Shadow Names)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T10:38:12-08:00","id":1191384,"title":"","content":"Should new mages be called simply 'Apprentice' - like in Mentor and Apprentice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T10:56:53-08:00","id":1191389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191185-cabal-theme-shadow-name?p=1191384#post1191384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should new mages be called simply 'Apprentice' - like in Mentor and Apprentice?</div> </div> </div> </div>That works, but if you want to sue it as an impromptu shadow name it needs a personal identifier. Perhaps just their mentor? &quot;Zarathustra's Apprentice&quot; isn't a great name, but works fine for referring to the person in third person and in direct conversation they can just be addressed as &quot;Apprentice&quot;.<br /> <br /> That also suggests a system where each master has only one full apprentice at a time and 'graduating' to journeyman status coincides with picking your Shadow Name, which could add another dimension to the problem where the characters' teachers are pressuring them to get over it already because they want to take on new charges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T11:11:34-08:00","id":1191396,"title":"","content":"I played in an online Mage Noir game where the player cabal settled on the name Lucky Six. (The setting was a Las Vegas stand-in; no points for guessing how many players we had to start \ud83d\ude09) While I don\u2019t think it ever came up in-character before the game fell apart, my personal view of the cabal symbolism was that each member stood for a number/side of a die. Cerberus, my Moros Guardian, would\u2019ve been \u201c3\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T11:40:18-08:00","id":1191404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191185-cabal-theme-shadow-name?p=1191384#post1191384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should new mages be called simply 'Apprentice' - like in Mentor and Apprentice?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends. The game already uses the word &quot;Apprentice&quot; and it refers to Mages who reached second dot in an Arcanum. The sequence goes thusly: Initiate - Apprentice - Disciple - Adept - Master. Mages might just use one of these titles if a Shadow Name is unavailable. However, calling an Initiate an Apprentice just asks for misunderstandings to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T16:43:38-08:00","id":1191475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191185-cabal-theme-shadow-name?p=1191404#post1191404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends. The game already uses the word &quot;Apprentice&quot; and it refers to Mages who reached second dot in an Arcanum. The sequence goes thusly: Initiate - Apprentice - Disciple - Adept - Master. Mages might just use one of these titles if a Shadow Name is unavailable. However, calling an Initiate an Apprentice just asks for misunderstandings to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly any mage who's hit the point where they can be represented as a starting character is at least a first-degree Apprentice.<br /> <br /> I feel like it's also worth remembering that basic Mage Status allows you to requisition an Alternate Identity in relatively little time, in the case of just needing a separate Wizard Identity for grounding out the Nimbus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T16:52:13-08:00","id":1191479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191185-cabal-theme-shadow-name?p=1191475#post1191475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I feel like it's also worth remembering that basic Mage Status allows you to requisition an Alternate Identity in relatively little time, in the case of just needing a separate Wizard Identity for grounding out the Nimbus.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, however the problem is also that unless you have Status 3, you can't requisition that Alternate Identity perpetually, so it'll soon be invalidated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}